#################################################################
# Connectedness repair (discipline v2.19.0, BP-D56 and BP-D57), 2026-10-19.
# The datatype properties the A-Box uses and nothing declared, then the relations
# between the chapter's subject branches that the chapter's own sources state.
#################################################################
chx:input a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "input expression"@en ; rdfs:comment "The expression an input/output example evaluates."@en ; rdfs:domain rd:IOExample ; rdfs:range xsd:string ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:output a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "output value"@en ; rdfs:comment "The value that evaluating the example expression gives."@en ; rdfs:domain rd:IOExample ; rdfs:range xsd:string ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:swapsRecipientOf a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "swaps the recipient that a signature commits to in"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Malware that swaps the recipient's address is the attack, and a signature covers the outputs it was made for. Basis: the chapter says of The device does not check the address: 'swap out the recipient's address'; the chapter says of Tampering breaks the signature: 'A signature covers the outputs'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:HardwareDoesNotCheckTheAddress ; rdfs:range chx:TamperBreaksSignature ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:explainsAddressOf a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "explains the different address of"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The same three keys in a different order under multi give another address, and the backup needs the full descriptor. Basis: the chapter says of The order in sortedmulti: 'multi with the same keys in two orders gave different addresses'; the chapter says of The descriptor is part of the backup: 'the same three keys in a different order under multi gave another address'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:SortedmultiOrder ; rdfs:range chx:DescriptorIsPartOfBackup ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:mentionsSameSuccessorAs a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "names the same SLIP39 as"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Both state that the book's chapter 5 lists or mentions SLIP39. Basis: the chapter says of Codex32 and SLIP39: 'the book's chapter 5 lists SLIP39 as a successor to BIP39'; the chapter says of Core has no mnemonics: 'the book's chapter 5 does mention SLIP39'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:Codex32AndSlip39 ; rdfs:range chx:CoreHasNoMnemonics ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:signsPsbtLike a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "signs a PSBT as in"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Both signings pass a PSBT between signers and finalize it. Basis: the chapter says of Two-of-three signing: 'the first key alone left the PSBT incomplete with 1 signature'; the chapter says of A PSBT through a cold node: 'took the unsigned PSBT of 528 characters'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:TwoOfThreeSigning ; rdfs:range chx:PsbtThroughColdNode ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:callsForNewBackupLike a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "calls for a new backup as the lesson of"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Encryption makes a new seed so a new backup is needed at once, and a stale backup misses later funds. Basis: the chapter says of Encryption makes a new seed: 'both say to make a new backup at once'; the chapter says of A stale backup misses funds: 'A backup does not know what happens after it'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:EncryptionMakesNewSeed ; rdfs:range chx:StaleBackupMissesFunds ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:keepsKeyOnPaperLike a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "keeps a private key on paper like"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A Casascius coin holds a private key on paper and a paper wallet is a single private key on paper. Basis: the chapter says of The Casascius hologram: 'a private key on paper under a tamper-evident hologram'; the chapter says of Paper wallets are obsolete: 'a single private key on paper'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:CasasciusHologram ; rdfs:range chx:PaperWalletsAreObsolete ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:failsAsCustodianLike a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "fails as a custodian like"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Both are exchanges whose wallet design failed. Basis: the chapter says of Bitfinex segregated wallets: 'a custodian's wallet design can fail'; the chapter says of The Mt. Gox loss: 'exchanges that concentrate user funds in a single hot wallet'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:BitfinexSegregatedWallets ; rdfs:range chx:MtGoxLoss ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:leavesUnrunDevice a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "records as not run"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The record lists the hardware device as not run. Basis: the chapter says of What was not executed: 'the hardware device'; the chapter says of External signer support: 'signs for a hardware device'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:WhatWasNotExecuted ; rdfs:range chx:ExternalSignerSupport ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:leavesUnrunPaper a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "records as not run"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The record lists paper and metal backups as not run. Basis: the chapter says of What was not executed: 'paper and metal backups'; the chapter says of Paper wallets are obsolete: 'a seed printed on paper'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:WhatWasNotExecuted ; rdfs:range chx:PaperWalletsAreObsolete ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:leavesUnrunBreach a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "records as not run"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The record lists an exchange breach as not run. Basis: the chapter says of What was not executed: 'an exchange breach'; the chapter says of The Mt. Gox loss: 'closed after losing 744,408 bitcoins'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:WhatWasNotExecuted ; rdfs:range chx:MtGoxLoss ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:leavesUnrunShamir a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "records as not run"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The record lists Shamir in a wallet as not run. Basis: the chapter says of What was not executed: 'Shamir in a wallet'; the chapter says of Shamir two-of-three: 'any two of them recovered the secret'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:WhatWasNotExecuted ; rdfs:range chx:ShamirTwoOfThree ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:leavesUnrunBip39 a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "records as not run"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The record lists BIP 39 recovery in Core as not run. Basis: the chapter says of What was not executed: 'BIP 39 recovery in Core'; the chapter says of Core has no mnemonics: 'Bitcoin Core does not use BIP 39 words'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:WhatWasNotExecuted ; rdfs:range chx:CoreHasNoMnemonics ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:leavesUnrunGpg a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "records as not run"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The record lists a good gpg verification as not run. Basis: the chapter says of What was not executed: 'a good gpg verification'; the chapter says of A signature needs keys: 'could call none of them good with an empty keyring'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:WhatWasNotExecuted ; rdfs:range chx:SignatureNeedsKeys ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:leavesUnrunBip324 a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "records as not run"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The record lists BIP 324 on the wire as not run. Basis: the chapter says of What was not executed: 'BIP 324 on the wire'; the chapter says of The v2 session on both sides: 'both reported the transport v2'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:WhatWasNotExecuted ; rdfs:range chx:V2SessionOnBothSides ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
chx:leavesUnrunEstate a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "records as not run"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The record lists estate planning with a lawyer as not run. Basis: the chapter says of What was not executed: 'estate planning with a lawyer'; the chapter says of The heir waits ten blocks: 'A script can give an heir a delayed path'."@en ;
    rdfs:domain chx:WhatWasNotExecuted ; rdfs:range chx:HeirWaitsTenBlocks ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/tbox> .
